<title>PORTUGAL: Portugal tax revenues seen rising 8.9 pct 1997.</title>
<headline>Portugal tax revenues seen rising 8.9 pct 1997.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1996-10-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Portugal's total tax receipts were expected to rise 8.9 percent in 1997 to 4,021.8 billion escudos, according to details of the budget presented to parliament.</p>
<p>The tax expected to show the sharpest increase in revenues is corporate tax, which should rise by 15.8 percent to 590.8 billion escudos, compared with 1996.</p>
<p>The ratio of taxation to income rose to 32.8 percent, that is 0.5 percentage point more than in 1996, &quot;due mainly to increased tax collection efficiency and economic growth,&quot; the budget draft said.</p>
<p>The Finance Ministry noted a decrease in the weighting of direct tax and an increase in the weighting of indirect tax in overall taxation.</p>
<p>PORTUGUESE TAX RECEIPTS, BILLION ESCUDOS</p>
<p>					  1996(1)     1997     Variation</p>
<p>----------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>    Direct taxes		    1,530.2    1,711.3   +11.8 pct</p>
<p>	 Income tax		   1,007.8    1,107.3    +9.9 pct</p>
<p>	 Corporate tax		  510.2	590.8   +15.8 pct</p>
<p>	 Others			    12.2	 13.2   +8.2 pct</p>
<p>----------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>    Indirect tax		    2,161.6    2,310.5    +6.7 pct</p>
<p>	 Fuel tax (ISP)		 452.5	481.1    +6.3 pct</p>
<p>	 VAT			    1,170.6    1,267.0    +8.2 pct</p>
<p>	 Car tax			  155.5	168.9    +8.6 pct</p>
<p>	 Tobacco tax		    164.0	174.1    +6.2 pct</p>
<p>	 Stamp duty		     179.0	178.3    -0.4 pct</p>
<p>	 Others			    40.0	 41.1    +2.8 pct</p>
<p>----------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>		Total taxes	    3,691.8    4,021.8    +8.9 pct</p>
<p>(1)Estimate</p>
